servings: 30
---

Combine @sugar{2%cups}, @butter{1/2%cups}, @milk{1/2%cups}, and @cocoa powder{4%Tbsp} in a #saucepan{}.

Heat to a rapid, rolling boil over medium-high heat. Let the fudge icing boil for ~{1%minute}. 

Remove from heat and stir in @vanilla extract{2%tsp}.

Whisk or beat the icing for ~{3-5%minutes} until the fudge is dark, glossy, and clinging to your whisk. The cooler it gets, the slower the icing will drip from your utensils.

Drop @Oreo cookies{30} into the icing and flip with tongs, ensuring the cookie is completely coated. Using tongs, allow icing to drip off Oreo to prevent having too much fudge.

Place each fudge-coated Oreo onto a parchment paper-lined baking sheet or work surface. Allow the coated cookies to cool completely so that the coating sets up.

Once set, if desired, trim away the excess and smooth out the edges.